div.p:
The Agreement. India won three concessions: 1) a
                    “no-war pact” intended to end Pakistan’s traditional policy of “confrontation”;
                    2) an agreement to resolve outstanding issues bilaterally, which will inhibit
                    any Pakistani attempts to bring the U.N. or other powers into future arguments;
                    and 3) Pakistani agreement to respect the present line of control in Kashmir as
                    the effective ceasefire line.
